{"ts": "2026-06-17T13:32:08+00:00", "note": "READY TO START. The PkgId threading it depends on is fully landed (2-32-3-9 HIR, 2-32-3-10 MIR, 2-32-3-11 codegen mangling). CURRENT MODEL: prefix_module (src/resolve.rs, AST-level pre-typing) rewrites *name -> module_name and is called from src/driver/sources/{implicit.rs,modules.rs} + driver/sources/mod.rs imports it. The HIR/MIR/codegen identity layer RECOVERS package ownership from the module_ name prefix that prefix_module stamps (hir::Program::owner_pkg_id matches \"<module>_\" prefixes against module_pkgs). RETIREMENT CAUTION: codegen mangling (mangle_symbol) currently ASSUMES func.name is \"<module>_<name>\" and owner_pkg_id ASSUMES the \"<module>_\" prefix exists. If prefix_module is removed, those recovery mechanisms break \u2014 must replace with carrying PkgId/module identity on the AST/HIR item directly (not via name prefix) BEFORE or ATOMIC-WITH removing the string prefixing. scope.md \u00a72.2: keep single-package fast path = root PkgId assigned to everything, behaves as today. Do this in a fresh focused effort."}
{"ts": "2026-06-17T14:05:09+00:00", "note": "DONE. Retired the prefix_module identity model. Identity was being re-derived per query via hir::Program::owner_pkg_id string-scan (starts_with \"<module>_\") \u2014 the last vestige of \"the prefix IS the identity\". Replaced with first-class carried attribution: new pkgid::build_item_pkgs() computes an exact item_symbol->PkgId map ONCE at HIR construction (after monomorphization), with longest-prefix-wins for nested module names. HIR/MIR field module_pkgs->item_pkgs; owner_pkg_id is now an exact map lookup. Renamed resolve::prefix_module -> flatten_module (it is now a pure namespace-flattening utility with NO identity semantics; renaming kept because it is the only namespace mechanism and \u00a72.2 requires single-package unchanged). codegen is_multi_package now keys on item_pkgs. 3 new build_item_pkgs unit tests + updated HIR/MIR identity tests. Build clean (zero warnings), 318 lib + all conformance pass, multi-module e2e smoke (use util -> util.double=42) works. NOTE: 3 pre-existing integration failures (column_max/min/sum @column store) confirmed failing on clean HEAD, unrelated."}
